Subject: [PATCH] hw/xen: set xenstore node owner to the domain running qemu
Upstream-Status: Pending

xenstore_mkdir() hardcodes dom0 as the owner of the nodes it creates:

    qemu_xen_xs_create(xenstore, 0, 0, xen_domid, p, path)
                                  ^ owner

libxenstore_create() turns that into an xs_set_permissions() call, and
xenstored refuses it for an unprivileged connection (tools/xenstored/core.c):

    /* Unprivileged domains may not change the owner. */
    if (domain_is_unprivileged(conn) &&
        perms.p[0].id != get_node_owner(node))
            return EPERM;

In a driver domain setup the device model is spawned by "xl devd" in an
unprivileged domain, so every xenstore_mkdir() below device-model/<domid>/
fails (the node is owned by the driver domain, not by dom0) and qemu logs:

    xen be core: xs_mkdir device-model/2: failed
    xen be core: xs_mkdir device-model/2/backends: failed
    xen be core: xs_mkdir device-model/2/backends/vkbd: failed
    xen be core: xs_mkdir device-model/2/backends/9pfs: failed

Note the message is misleading: xs_mkdir() itself succeeds, it is the
following xs_set_permissions() that fails.

Use the domain qemu is running in as the owner instead. It is read from the
relative "domid" node, which xenstored resolves against the caller's own
domain path. When the node is not readable - which is the case for dom0 -
fall back to 0 and keep the previous behaviour.

diff --git a/hw/xen/xen_pvdev.c b/hw/xen/xen_pvdev.c
--- a/hw/xen/xen_pvdev.c
+++ b/hw/xen/xen_pvdev.c
@@ -58,9 +58,32 @@ void xen_config_cleanup(void)
     }
 }
 
+/*
+ * The domain qemu is running in, which is not necessarily dom0: with a driver
+ * domain the device model is spawned by "xl devd" in an unprivileged domain.
+ */
+static unsigned int xenstore_self_domid(void)
+{
+    static unsigned int self_domid;
+    static bool self_domid_valid;
+    unsigned int len;
+    char *str;
+
+    if (!self_domid_valid) {
+        self_domid_valid = true;
+        str = qemu_xen_xs_read(xenstore, 0, "domid", &len);
+        if (str != NULL) {
+            self_domid = atoi(str);
+            free(str);
+        }
+    }
+    return self_domid;
+}
+
 int xenstore_mkdir(char *path, int p)
 {
-    if (!qemu_xen_xs_create(xenstore, 0, 0, xen_domid, p, path)) {
+    if (!qemu_xen_xs_create(xenstore, 0, xenstore_self_domid(), xen_domid, p,
+                            path)) {
         xen_pv_printf(NULL, 0, "xs_mkdir %s: failed\n", path);
         return -1;
     }
     xenstore_cleanup_dir(g_strdup(path));
     return 0;
 }
